r","feedback_revision":"3b3fe5a72a24fd1ad3b5b87c","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_curated20261026_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $f\\colon X\\to Y$ and $g\\colon W\\to Z$. Which condition is necessary and sufficient for $g(f(x))$ to define $g\\circ f$ on all of $X$, under the convention on this page?","options":["When the range of $g$ lies inside the domain of $f$","When $f$ and $g$ are defined on the same domain","When the range of $f$ lies inside the domain of $g$","Only when the range of $f$ equals the domain of $g$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7a615a9e2ec61d0922d27d7b","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_curated20261026_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"If $f\\colon X\\to Y$ and $g\\colon Y\\to Z$, what is the domain and codomain of $g\\circ f$?","options":["$g\\circ f\\colon Y\\to X$","$g\\circ f\\colon Z\\to X$","$g\\circ f\\colon X\\to Z$","$g\\circ f\\colon X\\to Y$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ef0b0ed6361fd5f5dbff09b8","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_curated20261026_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f\\colon\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$, $f(x) = x^2$, and $g\\colon\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$, $g(y) = y+1$. What is $(g\\circ f)(2)$?","options":["$9$","$5$","$3$","$4$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b70ab56e973f0416e8bd8ae6","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_composition_of_functions_e5a028fe_curated20261026_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f\\colon X\\to Y$ and $g\\colon W\\to Z$, with $Y\\ne W$. Which statement correctly determines whether $g\\circ f$ is defined on all of $X$?","options":["It is impossible whenever the two declared middle sets differ.","It is guaranteed whenever the two functions are real-valued.","It depends on whether the actual range of $f$ lies in $W$.","It is guaranteed whenever the domains $X$ and $W$ coincide."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6b68e24f56999c64437f368a","time_limit":35},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_curated20261026_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Does $g\\circ f=f\\circ g$ necessarily hold for two functions $f,g\\colon\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$?","options":["No; defined compositions can have different values.","Yes; every pair of real functions commutes.","Yes; equality holds whenever the two functions are different.","No; distinct functions can never commute."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"06b369450333558c66bb0fe8","time_limit":25},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_curated20261026_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For functions $f,g,h$ whose compositions are defined, which identity expresses associativity of composition?","options":["$(h\\circ g)\\circ f=h\\circ(g\\circ f)$","$g\\circ f=f\\circ g$","$f\\circ f=f$","$g\\circ f=g+f$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"35fb659feb1a9c1c9f7c4400","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_curated20261026_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For $f\\colon X\\to Y$, what is $f\\circ \\operatorname{id}_X$?","options":["$f$","$\\operatorname{id}_X$","$\\operatorname{id}_Y$","a constant function"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"33459d392906c0f243ca911d","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_010_composition_of_functions_curated20261026_009","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f\\colon X\\to Y$ and $g\\colon Y\\to Z$ be bijections. Which expression always gives $(g\\circ f)^{-1}\\colon Z\\to X$?","options":["$f^{-1}\\circ g^{-1}$","$g^{-1}\\circ f^{-1}$","$f\\circ g$","$g\\circ f$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a604a02e542690ec7c5a3d61","time_limit":30}]}}